About the Role
We are looking for an Event Specialist to plan, coordinate, and execute corporate and external events from end to end.
This person will be responsible not only for the execution of events, but also for understanding their impact and results, using data and insights to continuously improve the company's event strategy
Key Responsibilities

• Plan, organize, and execute corporate, industry, customer, partner, and internal events;

• Manage events from initial briefing and planning through execution and post-event activities;

• Develop timelines, checklists, budgets, and action plans;

• Manage and negotiate with vendors, agencies, venues, and partners;

• Coordinate event logistics and on-site operations;

• Curate and coordinate event agendas, including keynotes, panels, and presentations;

• Manage event experiences, including branded materials, giveaways, and attendee engagement initiatives;

• Coordinate Tenchi's participation in strategic trade shows, conferences, and industry events;

• Work closely with Marketing, Sales, and other internal teams to ensure events support business objectives;

• Support Sales through in-person activations and customer engagement initiatives;

• Coordinate regional initiatives aligned with target accounts (ABM) and support local market initiatives and industry presence;

• Monitor event performance and analyze results, including audience engagement, leads, business opportunities, and overall impact;

• Create event dashboards and performance reports to track results and identify insights and opportunities for improvement;

• Prepare post-event reports with key results, insights, and recommendations;

• Track event budgets and evaluate the return and effectiveness of initiatives;

• Maintain strong relationships with suppliers, partners, and stakeholders;

• Identify opportunities to improve event experience, efficiency, and business impact.

Requirements
Requirements

• Previous experience planning, producing, and managing events end to end, from initial planning through execution and post-event activities;

• Experience with vendors, agencies, budgets, and event logistics;

• Analytical mindset and ability to measure and communicate event results and business impact;

• Strong organizational and project management skills;

• Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills;

• Fluent English, both written and spoken;

• Ability to manage multiple priorities and work effectively under deadlines;

• Availability to travel and attend events on-site when required.

